    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Knowledge Base Ingestion (run this first)\nEdit the text in **Company Knowledge Base**, then click Execute once. The text is chunked, embedded with OpenAI and stored under the memory key `company_kb`.\n\nSwap **Simple Vector Store** for Pinecone or Qdrant for production persistence - the rest of the workflow stays identical.",
        "height": 448,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "7fa9c9ca-a5dd-460c-a4fd-a61aad4dae05",
      "name": "Sticky Note b68f0e1e",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1744,
        656
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Intake + RAG drafting\nGmail Trigger polls every minute for unread mail. **Normalize Email** flattens sender, subject and body into clean fields. The agent must call the vector store tool before answering, and returns structured JSON (reply, category, confidence, needs_human).\n\nTip: add a Gmail search query in the trigger filters (e.g. `to:support@yourcompany.com`) so only support mail fires this.",
        "height": 384,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "6213ea3c-7ea1-4b9a-aae2-7c84984f3ee6",
      "name": "Sticky Note 38185d9b",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -2000,
        832
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Human-in-the-loop + delivery\n**Ask Supervisor to Approve** pauses the execution and emails the draft with Approve / Reject buttons (12h timeout).\n\nApprove -> the reply is sent in the original thread.\nReject -> the draft is saved in Gmail for a human to edit and send.\n\nEither way the email is marked read so the trigger never reprocesses it.",
        "height": 288,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "865543fd-e94f-4f0c-a392-4c2bfbf4ebe3",
      "name": "Sticky Note 6a4ee361",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -2352,
        992
      ]
    }
